  :build-flags ["-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release" "-DGGML_NATIVE=ON" "-DGGML_OPENMP=ON"
                "-DGGML_VULKAN=OFF" "-DLLAMA_CURL=OFF" "-DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON"]
  :api-difference
  "Upstream replaced llama_model_params' use_mmap/use_mlock booleans with a
   single load_mode enum. The shim absorbs it -- native/Makefile probes
   llama.h for `enum llama_load_mode` and defines JL_HAS_LOAD_MODE, so one
   source builds against both APIs and jl_model_params keeps its two booleans.
   Probed rather than version-gated because llama.cpp exposes no API version
   macro. This is the ONLY difference the clean build required."
  :gate-result
  "PASSES. Logits bit-identical to the experimental build: token 11751 at
   -1.555883. M1 max_abs_dlogprob 0.00000000 at 4.01x, same 1-token BPE seam.
   State blob is 20263652 bytes here vs 20263632 on the fork -- a 20-byte
   serialization difference, which is why state carries an ABI and a model
   content id rather than being assumed portable."

  ;; ---- PRIOR EXPERIMENTAL COORDINATE, retained as evidence, NOT promoted
  :prior
  {:sha "390c307752ab78fd8189f359d6954c9ba1be74af"
   :subject "Fix build-cann workflow by adding placeholder job"
   :upstream-of "isHuangXin/llama.cpp (BitNet fork), vendored at BitNet/3rdparty/llama.cpp"
   :working-tree-dirty true
   :worktree-diff "docs/llamacpp-worktree.diff"
   :why-not-promoted
   "Two reasons. The captured diff is XDNA2/NPU offload for BitNet I2_S GEMMs,
    gated behind BITNET_XDNA_RUNTIME_DIR at build time and BITNET_XDNA=1 at
    runtime -- inert for Qwen3.5 Q4_0, which never takes the I2_S path -- so it
    was not NEEDED. And the commit is a FORK commit, not an upstream ancestor:
    `gh api repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commits/390c3077` resolves it only because
    forks share a commit network, and `compare` reports it as diverged. Its
    ggml-cpu CMakeLists references ../../../../src/ggml-bitnet-lut.cpp, a file
    in BitNet's parent tree, so it cannot build standalone at all. A dependency
    that only builds inside another project is not a promotion coordinate."}}

 :jolt-llama-results
 {:repo "casselc/jolt-llama"
  :final-branch "agent/onbox/v0-gate-oracle-correction"
  :promoted-surface
  "SINGLE-TOKEN candidate scoring. It reads every score from one base
   distribution, needs no candidate evaluation, no saved state and no rewind,
   and touches neither native state nor the token ledger -- so it cannot
   desynchronise, structurally. Multi-token scoring is EXPERIMENTAL: its
   numerical-base and atomicity holes are closed, but its guarantees rest on
   identity checks and a recovery path rather than on that structural argument."
  :state-coordinate
  "shim ABI + native runtime build id + model content sha256 + seq id 0 +
   exact token vector with an integrity SENTINEL + state byte count with a
   sampled sentinel. For candidate rewind additionally: the originating
   session id and evaluation revision, because token equality is not numerical
   equality."
  :integrity
  "REAL SHA-256 content digests, computed in the shim. :token-sha256 over the
   canonical little-endian int32 encoding, :state-sha256 over the whole blob.
   Verified against the published FIPS vectors in smoke.c before anything
   trusts them.
   Computed natively because the bytes are already there: feeding a 52 MiB blob
   to jolt-crypto's OpenSSL FFI measured ~47 000 ms, essentially all
   marshalling, against ~350 ms natively.
   The token digest is checked on every restore. The BLOB digest is checked for
   a state that did not originate in the restoring session; a same-session
   rewind skips it, because candidate rewind restores once per candidate and
   verifying each time cost ~345 ms and took the exact-spine speedup from 3.92x
   to 3.00x. verify-state-digest forces the full check."
  :concurrency
  "Handles are THREAD-CONFINED. Close is the exception: a CAS state machine
   admits one closer, and a failed native close lands on :close-failed rather
   than stranding at :closing. Runtime init is likewise CAS'd. Concurrent
   inference on one session is NOT supported and is not claimed."
  :reviewed-branch "agent/onbox/embedded-libllama-v0"
  :reviewed-sha "6ec88472bc63371ac9b70729ffbd58e35f35ce8d"
  :hardening-branch "agent/onbox/v0-safety-hardening"
  :note "The Samizdat embedded-controller canary was run against the reviewed
         sha and its evidence is not rewritten; the hardened coordinate is a
         separate one, regression-tested against that canary."}

